[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:It Could be Worse]
[00:06.41]Had the writer's money been stolen? | 作者的钱被偷了吗？
[00:14.34]I entered the hotel manager's office and sat down. | 我走进旅馆经理的办公室，坐了下来。
[00:19.84]I had just lost ￡50 and I felt very upset. | 我刚刚丢失了50英镑，感到非常沮丧。
[00:25.84]'I left the money in my room,' I said, 'and it's not there now. ' | “我把钱落在房间里了，”我说，“现在它不在那儿了。”
[00:32.96]The manager was sympathetic, but he could do nothing. | 经理深表同情，但他无能为力。
[00:38.46]'Everyone's losing money these days,' he said. | “现在大家都在丢钱，”他说。
[00:43.62]He started to complain about this wicked world but was interrupted by a knock at the door. | 他开始抱怨这个邪恶的世界，但被一阵敲门声打断了。
[00:52.00]A girl came in and put an envelope on his desk. | 一个女孩走了进来，在他的桌上放了一个信封。
[00:56.78]It contained ￡50. | 里面装着50英镑。
[00:59.54]'I found this outside this gentleman's room,' she said. | “我在这位先生的房间外面发现了这个，”她说。
[01:04.72]'Well,' I said to the manager,'there is still some honesty in this world!' | “噢，”我对经理说，“这世界上还是有诚实可言的！”